    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Boxes are sealed with high‑strength tape and marked with “Fragile” or “This Side Up” as needed.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>After packing, the items are carefully loaded onto the truck using dollies, straps, and protective blankets. We double‑check weight distribution to keep the vehicle balanced and compliant with Denver’s traffic regulations. Throughout transit, our drivers use GPS monitoring and real‑time updates so you can track the route and estimated arrival time.</p>

<p>Upon arrival at the destination, the uncrating phase begins. The crew unloads in the same order they loaded, placing boxes and furniture directly onto their designated spots.</p>
<p>We then unpack each room, setting up furniture, reconnecting appliances, and ensuring all items are in their correct locations. Finally, we conduct a quality‑check walk‑through with you to confirm that every item has arrived intact and that the new space feels ready for you to settle in.</p></div>
